                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First, I really, really like both text story games and zombies. So, I just KNEW I was going to like this game. But…I just didn’t. I spent an hour and a half for one playthrough, that I took my time doing, by the way, and I can’t remember anything about it. There were no interesting or unique things about it. I remember thinking that these characters were winey and the storyline was SO typical. Like is this a story or a bunch of stereotypes throw together? It didn’t even have achievements.\n I also remember that since I got the Delta Force Operator I wanted to use it (even in just my first playthrough), so as a female I chose that as my profession and the game says something like “oh you’re a delta operator? That means you’re actually a dude right? Did you accidently click to play as a woman lol? So let me ask you again if you actually want to play as a guy because women aren’t Bad A enough to actually be bosses.” I’m not even kidding people. Then it gives this “oh you actually ARE a woman, oh well screw the rules. We’ll LET you do it.” I’m REALLY not kidding, this isn’t exactly what was said, but it’s clear what they meant: If you are a Delta Operator, they expect you to be a male because a woman can’t handle it in anything but a video game (I don't care if there are restrictions currently in place, we should NOT reinforce this idea even in a game!). This should have been the refund point. But nope. I had to keep going to see if it got better. It did not and I have no desire to play it again and see how it branched out.\n\nI paid for the game AND DLC and now know why the only good review was from the guy who got it for free. I expected better from a “Choice of” Game.   : ^ / \n",
